{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1197049-2e-gifted-from-mcg-fan-update","id":1197049,"title":"[2E] Gifted from MCG fan update","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-18T22:52:25-07:00","id":1197049,"title":"[2E] Gifted from MCG fan update","content":"I think about including Gifted - 'magical scientists' template from <b>Mage Chronicler's Guide</b> - as players option to choose from. However there are some problems with reworking their mechanics to <b>Mage </b>2E .<br /> 1. <b>How to recreate Reach in Gifted?</b> Like they would made much more unstable Supernal Experiments ( their practice of spells )?<br /> 2. <b>I wonder how to deal with Supernal Mysteries and related Arcana Attainments - like Mage Sight and Supernal Summoning - for them. </b>Gifted, at least in 1E <b>MGC</b>, are Pathless. They do not have Mage Sight. They do not have Supernal Beings to summon. If <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/walking-in-the-world-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">Aedes ( from <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> )</a> are in Supernal World of each Realm - they will not be able to perceive them. So should I open to Gifted 'glimpses' general Supernal? Or just let other Paths share their Mage Sight? Maybe just give Gifted alternate general Arcana Attainments instead of Mage Sight and Summoning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T00:31:22-07:00","id":1197067,"title":"","content":"Not sure Mage needs another lesser template.<br /> Just make an Obrimos-Matter Proximus dynasty about finding the hidden laws of reality, and call it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T00:40:51-07:00","id":1197071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1197049-2e-gifted-from-mcg-fan-update?p=1197067#post1197067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure Mage needs another lesser template.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not Lesser Template - it's 'weird science' alternative Awakened template. They are like mages, only based on Supernal Science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-19-2018, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T01:02:28-07:00","id":1197080,"title":"","content":"Okay, well that sounds like a Obrimos/Moros Mage with an interesting Legacy, and/or scientific Dedication.<br /> <br /> Also claiming that's an 'alternate' Mage template is a bit weird, considering the Supernal encompasses the scientific method.<br /> Moros and to a lesser extent Obrimos Mages use (and surpass) scientific tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T01:13:08-07:00","id":1197084,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12644_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12644\" data-vbnamecard=\"12644\">HerbertIsBestBert</a> - Gifted are from <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/82216/Mage-Chroniclers-Guide\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Mage Chronicler's Guide</b></a> - big book of <b>Mage</b> game Hacks and chronicles ideas...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T02:26:26-07:00","id":1197093,"title":"","content":"Try searching for \u201cTechnocratic Utopias\u201d in this (Awakening) forum. (On phone, can\u2019t link) Basically they have the five Conventions of the Technocracy remodeled as a science-y version of the five Paths. You could mine them for ideas (especially if you want the Gifted to have full Path functions like Mage Sight)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T02:58:12-07:00","id":1197099,"title":"","content":"<b>Hermit</b>, I thank for this idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I remember reading those \u201cTechnocratic Utopias\u201d some time ago. But I would still stay with more original idea of Gifted as basically Pathless.<br /> <br /> So question can be remodeled - <b>How could you make Pathless in 2E Mage?</b> Is it even possible, with all the need of Supernal World implication of Awakened magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T03:16:46-07:00","id":1197105,"title":"","content":"Yes. You just tell your players to ignore Paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T03:20:49-07:00","id":1197109,"title":"","content":"No if you mix Gifted with Awakened - like the Hack points is possible in 1E games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T03:27:25-07:00","id":1197112,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re getting your threads confused now you\u2019ve made so many of them. You meant to respond to me in your creation of the FC thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T07:56:28-07:00","id":1197194,"title":"","content":"Isn't just the easiest way to make them mages that don't believe in the occult and supernal in the ways other mages understand it? Maybe just slap a Persistent Condition on them that allows them to use magic, but only if they incorporate a Environmental Yantra in the spell. This would for the 'scientists' be a laboratory, and then give them the Techn\u00e9 merit with the theme of 'science'.<br /> No need for a lesser template, no need to change any rules, no need to house rule everything, no need to cross over, no difference in power between PCs etc etc. <br /> <br /> But if you remove paths, you should probably remove them altogether and change the cosmology as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T08:38:52-07:00","id":1197211,"title":"","content":"Well, the problem is that wouldn\u2019t allow for having cake and eating it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T08:49:57-07:00","id":1197217,"title":"","content":"My own preference is to use the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e\">Other Five Paths</a> for the Gifted (see the <i>Science and Magic</i> heading in the first post). That said, your preference is Pathless; so let's go with that. <br /> <br /> MCG's Gifted had Mage Sight; it just wasn't aspected to a particular Supernal Realm. Being Pathless meant that you couldn't do Astral Sojourns; so your <i>only</i> contact with the Supernal was through Mystery Plays (i.e., Mage Sight). With 2e's changes to Mage Sight, \u201cPathless\u201d would sever that as well, according to a literal reading. <br /> <br /> I'll have to think about this some more; I'll get back to you later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T11:15:51-07:00","id":1197271,"title":"","content":"OK: the Gifted have Insight rather than Gnosis. Insight doesn't affect your perceptions: the whole business of <i>Gnosis by Path</i> (pp.84\u201385) doesn't apply to Insight. It's possible that Insight doesn't raise Attribute caps; or maybe it does. Who knows?<br /> <br /> Vision (the Gifted counterpart to Mana) becomes vital in a Pathless setup: as there are no Ruling Colleges, improvising an experiment always costs Vision. Pattern Restoration may not be a thing for the Gifted, except in a limited way of dealing with mental Conditions. Likewise, it seems unlikely that a Gifted can Scour her Pattern or engage in a Blood Sacrifice to gain Vision. <br /> <br /> Nimbus becomes more important, as the lack of Paths and Ruling Arcana leaves fewer things to personalize the scientist's experiences. In many ways, Nimbus replaces Path.<br /> <br /> High Speech is unchanged.<br /> <br /> Mage Sight: the Gifted don't have this. Instead, they must use Knowing and Unveiling experiments to achieve these effects. <br /> <br /> Summoning Supernal Entities: likewise, the Gifted don't have an innate ability to summon Supernal Entities; they must improvise suitable experiments to do so. That said, summoning circles aren't really a thing that scientists do. When it does come up, tailor the summoned entity according to the scientist's Nimbus. <br /> <br /> Likewise with Soulstones: the Gifted generally don't deal in matters pertaining to the soul. When they do, it's through experiments involving the College of Morbid Studies. <br /> <br /> Astral Sojourns are likewise done via experiments in the College of Essential and Advanced Psychology, rather than being something the Gifted can just do. <br /> <br /> Finally, all experiments <i>require</i> the use of a suitable Tool, almost certainly an Order Tool. The upside is that that Tool doesn't count against Insight's Yantra limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T11:48:09-07:00","id":1197279,"title":"","content":"So with lack of Mage Sight and Supernal Summoning for Gifted - maybe giving them replacing Collage Attainments? Maybe stuff about locking experiments in machines ( i.e. creating Imbued Items from any Collage, not only Prime one)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-19-2018, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T12:22:34-07:00","id":1197290,"title":"","content":"Given the number of capabilities that the Gifted don't have, including the three-dot Attainment, I could see replacing it with a broader version of the four-dot Prime Attainment, as you suggest. It does leave the question as to what replaces said four-dot Attainment, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T12:36:09-07:00","id":1197295,"title":"","content":"Spellcasting? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I.E. That Prime 4th dot Collegium Attainment would let Gifted to 'plan' the experiment, not doing it as Tool. It would like as geomancy ritual casting when classical mage is hanging over map of local and do some words to target with spells those on the premise. Think of Supernal Scientists doing something like that, without need to build Tool for experiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}